<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Dual citizenship means Germany now in competition for talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee69ff97617679f7d9bc1d4e9d57b8b5847f41f8a92c86a564314185b73d22c8</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797--d43696518a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Coach Jürgen Klopp has named several players to his first Germany squad who are eligible to play for other countries. Some still aren't committed to playing for thje national team long-term.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Germany's football team to 'reclaim the flag'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:057736f0b24fd2dd61dde9254b14a2640f7c867b2712f312a03d4ecaa0741b0f</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-germany-s-football-team-to-reclaim-the-flag/a-79307610--57ff88db5991.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-germany-s-football-team-to-reclaim-the-flag/a-79307610?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp, Germany's new head coach, says he wants his team to reclaim pride in being German after recent political developments.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp's first Germany squad includes 44 players</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:551d1b650f12c757eb77a028f394d92f0ffdb8fbe0b65d8b7d298434702c0cee</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-s-first-germany-squad-includes-44-players/a-79289254--9874c23792d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-s-first-germany-squad-includes-44-players/a-79289254?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's new head coach Jürgen Klopp has named a huge squad for his first four games, splitting them into two groups. A host of new faces is included.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>VAR's mission creep a problem for football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c5cbd0ce7cd2017d5b455f6099b97014c7658c6284f74683ce14255e955fb30</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642--644b469bed29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a decade of use, questions around VAR in football are louder than ever. Has the technology strayed too far from its remit?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Ovechkin backs Putin party in campaign video</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4af5867e016c652ec522fc850a60f9374eac5174463573954c932ca19e349e1b</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772--a8049deceb76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey legend Alexander Ovechkin has lent Vladimir Putin's party a helping hand in its parliamentary election campaign. That's in keeping with a pattern of support by an athlete who claims not to be political.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>After Neuer: Who will be Germany's new No. 1 goalkeeper?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce415e00693ef86d0fdbbcbc5ae28a0833ee1b6d7d24f3f1d1f01a1c0f5c93d3</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377--1d35484fc587.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following Manuel Neuer's retirement, there are many candidates to succeed him, but which goalkeeper will Jürgen Klopp choose? What factors will play a role? And will Neuer's future have an indirect influence?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Women's Basketball World Cup: Can Germany harness a boom?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:594c7e668cc578b49ffdb47d88eeeb4441bddddcf4fe70eba4586b36ff0d5bc1</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602--77d972e02866.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany thrilled fans at the Women's Basketball World Cup. But even if this sparked a boom in the women's game, the infrastructure simply isn't ready for it.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Zverev wins US Open in golden year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:435bc764fb1c3794bbf2c8a8b578e6e0a3971b32c3a0dbed1e0cabd547f77da4</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T22:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706--d962ccd6a0c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev has won the US Open for the first time, defeating Ben Shelton in the final. It is Zverev's second Grand Slam win of 2026 after a long wait for his first title, but controversy still hangs over him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU sports commissioner says FIFA is 'damaging to football'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e90b6d59a2e3c675848910ff0c873dfdda580ca17391be813bbe36a0d601bb91</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424--c7a4bd30a298.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Speaking to DW, EU Commissioner Glenn Micallef hit out at world football's governing body over its "poor governance."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Afghanistan's women: A national soccer team without a home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74df50533b287be4dad607760acae0df2802108062a69ba0e7135025ef17eb01</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500--7cfb666b9c3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Afghan women's national football team has finally been officially recognized by FIFA. Now the players want to make history both on and off the field.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Egg freezing in women's football: Choice or pressure?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8771eb3f942cdfdb8c736d245914e9087ab2a43c60b33f2ee6e5dd31f3642445</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egg-freezing-in-women-s-football-choice-or-pressure/a-79145259--8a56ba698069.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egg-freezing-in-women-s-football-choice-or-pressure/a-79145259?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's football federation is set to join a handful of clubs in paying for female players to freeze their eggs. Experts have welfare concerns.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
